📅 Day 7 – Introduction to Arrays

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on the concept of arrays in Java. The mentor explained how arrays are used to store multiple values of the same data type in a single variable, making data management more efficient and organized.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to Arrays

Definition of an array

Importance of arrays in storing multiple values

Memory allocation and index-based storage

Understanding that array indexing starts from 0

2️⃣ Array Declaration and Initialization

Syntax for declaring an array

Different ways to initialize arrays

Allocating memory using the new keyword

Assigning values at the time of declaration

3️⃣ Accessing Array Elements

Using index values to access elements

Understanding arrayName[index]

Importance of index boundaries

Avoiding ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException

4️⃣ Traversing Arrays

Using for loop to iterate through arrays

Understanding array length using .length property

Accessing each element sequentially

5️⃣ Basic Array Operations

Searching elements

Modifying elements

Updating values at specific index positions

🎯 Learning Outcome

Understood the purpose and structure of arrays.

Learned how to declare, initialize, and access array elements.

Gained clarity on traversing arrays using loops.

Practiced basic operations like searching and updating values.

Strengthened foundational knowledge for handling collections of data.